{
  "schema": "orfs.recovery.checkpoints.v1",
  "method": "for each workload and size 2^k committed bytes: build a volume, take an index checkpoint, then time (a) full replay, (b) checkpoint + suffix replay (log-scan discovery), (c) directory-assisted discovery, and report bytes/records replayed and Go heap (runtime.MemStats).",
  "note": "Go heap (HeapInuse) and Go runtime Sys are reported, not process RSS. Each timed arm is the minimum of `reps` runs. volume.Open still scans the authoritative log to establish the committed root in every arm; the checkpoint bounds only the index reconstruction. Absolute times are single-host and sensitive to cache/GC state.",
